# Never commit credentials
*.openai-key
apikey*
*.pfx
*.pem

# OS noise
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
~$*

# Never commit real student data.
# Marking runs drop roll/ledger files next to the skill; these carry names,
# student IDs and enrolment status pulled from WiseNet. Fixtures under
# examples/ are fictional and ARE committed - these patterns are the backstop
# for live working files only.
mk*roll.json
*_roll.json
rpt_WiseNET*
*.xls

# Nothing from an auditor RUN belongs in here. An assurance ledger and its
# deliverables describe an RTO's compliance failures in detail and often name
# staff. They stay in the working folder on the RTO's own machine.
assurance*.json
deliverables/
00-document-register.md
01-gap-analysis*
02-uplifted-policies/
04-compliance-calendar*
06-risk-register*
08-verification-report.md

# Working backups kept beside the scripts - not part of any skill
*.bak
*.bak2
*.orig
.bak-*/

# Dated working backups a skill run drops beside its own files. Git already
# keeps the history, so committing these just doubles the repo.
*-backup-2[0-9][0-9][0-9][0-9][0-9][0-9][0-9]*
*.backup-2[0-9][0-9][0-9][0-9][0-9][0-9][0-9]*

# Google service-account key the resource-production skill reads - never commit it
service-account*.json
